Meg Donnelly, who co-starred alongside Jeffery as Addison in the franchise, shared an emotional tribute Thursday (Sept. 3), admitting that she&#8217;s had to process the news.

&#8220;I have been in a state of denial,&#8221; Donnelly wrote. &#8220;I feel like I keep waiting for something before I believe it&#8217;s actually real.&#8221;

Donnelly went on to remember Jeffery as &#8220;truly one of a kind,&#8221; praising her strength, sense of humor and care for the people she loved. &#8220;God, there is no one like her,&#8221; she added.

Though Donnelly said posting about such a devastating loss felt &#8220;strange and unnatural,&#8221; she ultimately thought about what Jeffery would have wanted, which was a collection of memories filled with the smiles, laughter and love she so often brought to others. &#8220;So, here you go my beautiful Carla,&#8221; Donnelly concluded. &#8220;Thank you for being such a huge part of my life. I love you always. Addi & Bree forever.&#8221;

View this post on Instagram

Milo Manheim, who starred as Zed opposite Donnelly&#8217;s Addison, also shared a series of photos and videos of Jeffery on his Instagram Story.

&#8220;Love you Carlaboo,&#8221; he wrote on one tribute. &#8220;The sweetest, kindest, most loving person.&#8221;

In another upload to his Story, Manheim thanked her for &#8220;spreading so much joy,&#8221; while an Instagram comment he left on the announcement of her death simply read, &#8220;Carla. The sweetest person I have ever met. I love you.&#8221;

Chandler Kinney, who portrayed Willa in the ZOMBIES films, similarly reflected on Jeffery&#8217;s unmistakable energy in a lengthy Instagram tribute.

&#8220;This doesn&#8217;t feel real,&#8221; she began, calling Jeffery &#8220;the sweetest, most sparkly gal&#8221; and writing that she made &#8220;every day better and brighter&#8221; with her positivity. Kinney also connected the actress&#8217; personality to the character she played, writing that part of the reason Jeffery brought so much &#8220;effervescence&#8221; to Bree was because &#8220;that&#8217;s really who you were in your heart.&#8221;

&#8220;A bubbly, vivacious heart-of-gold cheerleader who loved nothing more than to uplift those around her,&#8221; Kinney continued. &#8220;I feel so grateful to have known your love.&#8221;

Kinney further honored her friend through a series of Instagram Stories, sharing photos and videos of their time together, including footage of Jeffery doing the splits in her cheerleading uniform. &#8220;If you knew her, you knew this was her signature move,&#8221; Kinney wrote. &#8220;The most joyous person.&#8221;

She also reposted memories of Jeffery with the ZOMBIES cast, noting that the actress &#8220;loved zombies with her whole heart.&#8221;

Kylee Russell, another member of the franchise&#8217;s cast, shared a collage of photos with Jeffery and wrote, &#8220;Oh Carla. I&#8217;m so blessed to have known you and call you my sister. I love you so much. And I will miss you for a lifetime.&#8221;

ZOMBIES actor Trevor Tordjman remembered Jeffery as &#8220;truly one of a kind,&#8221; writing on Instagram that he would &#8220;never forget&#8221; her energy.

The outpouring of love went further than the cast&#8217;s individual tributes, and spread throughout the comments section of the announcement posted to Jeffery&#8217;s official Instagram account by her talent management team. Pearce Joza wrote, &#8220;I love you, Carla,&#8221; while Ariel Martin (Baby Ariel) shared her disbelief and repeatedly expressed her admiration and love for her former co-star.

&#8220;I&#8217;m in shock,&#8221; wrote Jadah Marie. &#8220;What a beautiful soul. I&#8217;m so heartbroken.&#8221;

Liamani, who has appeared in Descendants: The Rise of Red and Camp Rock 3 , wrote, &#8220;Sweet girl. Knowing you was an honor. There will never be another soul like yours.&#8221; ZOMBIES 4 actress Swayam Bhatia added, &#8220;Rest in peace Carla. We love you.&#8221;

Actor Tony Nappo remembered Jeffery as a &#8220;warm young, talented woman full of life and positivity,&#8221; while Camryn Manheim, mother of ZOMBIES alum Milo Manheim, wrote that her &#8220;heart is so heavy&#8221; over the news.

ZOMBIES 4 actress Freya Skye wrote in the comments: &#8220;“what a wonderful, bright, joyous human. Rest easy Carla.&#8221;

Jeffery&#8217;s death was announced Wednesday by Alexanders Talent Management, which said the actress died Tuesday at age 33. The company remembered her as a &#8220;beautiful, vibrant, and incredibly talented woman whose radiant smile could light up any room.&#8221;
